---
/*
  PAGE GOAL: Homepage. REVISED 2026-07-26, Round 3, per owner rejection
  of the Round-2 build:
    (a) Hero read as messy and the headline was too long — replaced
        with the recommended short, numberless, single-beat headline
        option (Option 1 of 3 in the copy file; owner picks the final
        wording at review). Hero.astro itself was also tightened
        (narrower container, tighter spacing, removed dead unused
        overflow-hidden/z-10 scaffolding) since the rejection was as
        much visual as textual.
    (b) The "capability strips" section misread the direction — six
        single-fact rows was not what was asked. Restored the ORIGINAL
        achievements-strip presentation (bordered stats-row, several
        numbers side by side, each with one line of context) the owner
        explicitly liked — now repeated ONCE PER CASE STUDY (4 strips),
        each linking to its case study/product page. See
        AchievementsStrip.astro (replaces CapabilityStrips.astro, which
        is now deleted — it had zero remaining callers).

  REVISED 2026-08-01, Round 4, per owner feedback on the round-3 build:
    (c) Hero headline swapped to the owner's own verbatim line
        ("The only thing holding your business is you and a
        spreadsheet?") — see the copy file's Hero section, updated
        2026-08-01. Subhead/CTA unchanged.
    (d) Strips made more compact (tighter panel padding, stat-grid
        gaps, and margins; stat value size stepped down one notch) and
        each strip now gets its own tinted, bordered panel — 4 colors
        from the existing palette (brand/gold/slate/muted, the same
        family `.badge-*` already uses), so the section reads as 4
        distinct blocks instead of one flat stack.

  REVISED 2026-08-03, Round 5, per owner review of the round-4 build:
    (e) Hero headline finalized with "together" (now: "The only thing
        holding your business together is you and a spreadsheet?").
    (f) Round 4's tints read as "badly colored (AI weak colors)" — too
        washed-out. Panels are now solid, confidently colored, and
        theme-invariant (see AchievementsStrip.astro's round-5 notes
        and the `.strip-panel*` classes in global.css for the full
        color-distance/contrast math behind the fix). Stat value size
        stepped down again. Section intro label and closing-note
        register changed to "Real business, real results." (the old
        "nothing invented/rounded" phrasing contradicted the `~`-
        prefixed figures already in use, per the copy file).
    (g) Copy finalized: fuel strip drops its "1 week" stat (3 stats
        now, not 4); travel strip has a new subline and new stats (2,
        8, ~10 hours a week); marketing strip's placeholders are
        resolved with real owner numbers (6 → 1, 20+ people,
        ~$56,000). Reception's placeholders are still pending an owner
        decision — untouched, byte-identical to round 4.

  REVISED 2026-08-04, Round 6 — FINAL styling pass, owner ships
  tomorrow — per owner review of the round-5 build:
    (h) Fills were too dark/muddy (`gold-800` read "brownishly bad").
        Moved to bright, saturated, opaque fills (brand-300, gold-400,
        slate-400) with dark text for AA instead of round 5's deep
        fills with light text — see AchievementsStrip.astro's round-6
        notes and the `.strip-panel*` classes in global.css for the
        distance/contrast math.
    (i) Section made visibly more compact: panels now sit in a 3-across
        row at sm+ (not stacked full-width blocks), padding/gaps/text
        sizes all tightened further than round 4's "compact" baseline.
    (j) Section intro changed to "Some projects we did for clients —
        real businesses, real results." (replaces "Real business, real
